  {
   "id": "uncertainty",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 0,
   "y": 2750,
   "width": 500,
   "height": 330,
   "color": "2",
   "text": "### Uncertainty<br><br>- A single autonomic measurement has weak interpretive power<br>- Transmitter names do not map to moods<br>- Cortisol is one signal among many"
  },
  {
   "id": "hypothesis",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 560,
   "y": 2750,
   "width": 560,
   "height": 330,
   "color": "6",
   "text": "### Open questions<br><br>- How do volume transmission and glial signalling complicate the synaptic model?<br>- Which dopamine measurements distinguish pathway-specific effects in humans?<br>- How well do animal arousal findings transfer to human cognition?"
  },
  {
   "id": "evidence-basis",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 1180,
   "y": 2750,
   "width": 600,
   "height": 430,
   "color": "4",
